<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31305" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσβαίνω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go on board</i> a ship, mostly abs., <i>embark,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.13
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς [πεντηκόντερον]</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.41
				</span></i>
			 : c. acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκάφος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					686
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>enter,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς κόρης νυμφεῖον εἰ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					1205
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δόμους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					380
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ. κακά</span>
			<i>come into</i> miseries, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				997
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτης ἄβυσσον πέλαγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					470
				</span></i>
			 ; reversely, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμοὶ γὰρ οἶκτος.. εἰσέβη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					298
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κἀμὲ γὰρ τὸ δυσχερὲς τοῦτ᾽
					εἰσβέβηκεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hyps.Fr.</u>
					5(3).20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>come in, be imported,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσέβαινον ἰσχάδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					117
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>project into,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				PTeb.
				86.24
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii B.C.)</span>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> causal in aor. 1, <i>make to go into, put
				into,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς δ᾽ ἑκατόμβην βῆσε θεῷ</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς νῆα</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.310
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				1055
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ba.</u>
				466
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ληΐδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.167
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
